# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Define the problem as an objective function {#step-1-define-the-problem-as-an-objective-function}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: Tukuyin ang problema bilang objective function {#step-1-define-the-problem-as-an-objective-function}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Optimization Solver accepts either an objective function or a graph as input. In this tutorial, the Ising spin glass minimization problem is defined as an objective function, and it has been tailored for the heavy-hex topology of IBM&reg; devices.\n"
msgstr "Ang Optimization Solver ay tumatanggap ng objective function o graph bilang input. Sa tutorial na ito, ang Ising spin glass minimization problem ay tinukoy bilang objective function, at ito ay inayos para sa heavy-hex topology ng mga IBM&reg; device.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because this objective function contains cubic, quadratic, and linear terms, it falls into the HOBO class of problems, known to be considerably more complicated to solve than conventional quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problems.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang objective function na ito ay naglalaman ng cubic, quadratic, at linear terms, ito ay nabibilang sa HOBO class ng mga problema, na kilalang mas kumplikado kaysa sa mga conventional quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problems.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For detailed discussion of the construction of the problem definition and previous results obtained from the Optimization Solver refer to [this technical manuscript](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.01743). The problem was originally defined and evaluated as part of a [paper published by Los Alamos National Laboratory](https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00997), and it has been adapted to leverage the full device width of the 156-qubit IBM Quantum Heron processors.\n"
msgstr "Para sa detalyadong talakayan ng konstruksiyon ng problem definition at mga nakaraang resultang nakuha mula sa Optimization Solver, sumangguni sa [technical manuscript na ito](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.01743). Ang problema ay orihinal na tinukoy at sinuri bilang bahagi ng isang [paper na inilathala ng Los Alamos National Laboratory](https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00997), at ito ay inangkop upang gamitin ang buong device width ng 156-qubit IBM Quantum Heron processors.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size {#calculate-the-function-size}"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang function size {#calculate-the-function-size}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function size depends on the number of binary decision variables and the interaction density. For the criteria of each size, see [Function sizes](/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver#function-sizes) in the Optimization Solver guide. Use the following helper to select `\"S\"`, `\"M\"`, or `\"L\"` without submitting a job. Count each distinct pair of variables that appears together in an objective term. A cubic term contributes three pairs, and pairs that appear in multiple terms are counted only once.\n"
msgstr "Ang function size ay depende sa bilang ng binary decision variables at sa interaction density. Para sa mga pamantayan ng bawat size, tingnan ang [Function sizes](/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver#function-sizes) sa Optimization Solver guide. Gamitin ang sumusunod na helper para pumili ng `\"S\"`, `\"M\"`, o `\"L\"` nang hindi nagsa-submit ng job. Bilangin ang bawat natatanging pares ng variables na magkasamang lumalabas sa isang objective term. Ang cubic term ay nag-aambag ng tatlong pares, at ang mga pares na lumalabas sa maraming term ay isang beses lang binibilang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Run the hybrid algorithm using the Fire Opal Optimization Solver {#step-2-run-the-hybrid-algorithm-using-the-fire-opal-optimization-solver}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: Patakbuhin ang hybrid algorithm gamit ang Fire Opal Optimization Solver {#step-2-run-the-hybrid-algorithm-using-the-fire-opal-optimization-solver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now use the Optimization Solver quantum function to run the algorithm. Behind the scenes, the Optimization Solver takes care of mapping the problem to a hybrid quantum algorithm, running the quantum circuits with error suppression, and performing the classical optimization.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, gamitin ang Optimization Solver quantum function upang patakbuhin ang algorithm. Sa likod ng eksena, ang Optimization Solver ay nag-aalaga sa pagmamapa ng problema sa isang hybrid quantum algorithm, pinapatakbo ang mga quantum circuit na may error suppression, at gumaganap ng classical optimization.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check to ensure that the chosen device has at least 156 qubits.\n"
msgstr "Suriin upang matiyak na ang napiling device ay may hindi bababa sa 156 qubits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Solver accepts a string representation of the objective function.\n"
msgstr "Ang Solver ay tumatanggap ng string representation ng objective function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size from the polynomial's variables and distinct interacting pairs, then pass the returned value to `solver.run` through `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang function size mula sa mga variable ng polynomial at sa mga natatanging nag-iinteract na pares, pagkatapos ay ipasa ang ibinalik na value sa `solver.run` sa pamamagitan ng `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your quantum function workload's status:\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang status ng workload ng iyong quantum function:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Solver returns a dictionary with the solution and associated metadata, such as the solution bitstring, number of iterations, and mapping of variables to bitstring. For a full definition of the Solver's inputs and outputs, check out the [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/api-reference).\n"
msgstr "Ang Solver ay nagbabalik ng dictionary na may solusyon at kaugnay na metadata, tulad ng solution bitstring, bilang ng iterations, at pagmamapa ng mga variable sa bitstring. Para sa buong kahulugan ng mga input at output ng Solver, tingnan ang [dokumentasyon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/api-reference).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Evaluate results {#step-3-evaluate-results}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Suriin ang mga resulta {#step-3-evaluate-results}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Solver found the correct solution, which was validated using classical optimization software. The complexity of this utility-scale problem requires an advanced optimization software to be solved classically, such as [IBM ILOG CPLEX Optimization Studio (CPLEX)](https://www.ibm.com/products/ilog-cplex-optimization-studio) or [Gurobi Optimization](https://www.gurobi.com/).\n"
"As a visual analysis of the quality of results, you can plot the results by calculating the cost values from the bitstrings and their probabilities. For comparison, plot the results alongside a distribution of randomly sampled bitstrings, which is equivalent to a \"brute-force\" classical solution. If the algorithm consistently finds lower costs, it suggests the quantum algorithm is effectively solving the optimization problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Natagpuan ng Solver ang tamang solusyon, na na-validate gamit ang classical optimization software. Ang pagiging kumplikado ng utility-scale problem na ito ay nangangailangan ng advanced optimization software upang malutas nang classically, tulad ng [IBM ILOG CPLEX Optimization Studio (CPLEX)](https://www.ibm.com/products/ilog-cplex-optimization-studio) o [Gurobi Optimization](https://www.gurobi.com/).\n"
"Bilang visual analysis ng kalidad ng mga resulta, maaari ninyong i-plot ang mga resulta sa pamamagitan ng pagkalkula ng cost values mula sa mga bitstring at ng kanilang mga probability. Para sa paghahambing, i-plot ang mga resulta kasama ng distribution ng random na sampled bitstrings, na katumbas ng isang \"brute-force\" na classical solution. Kung ang algorithm ay patuloy na nakakahanap ng mas mababang costs, ipinapahiwatig nito na epektibong nilulutas ng quantum algorithm ang optimization problem.\n"

